## Core Components

### 1. The Nexus — Master Orchestrator ([nexus.py](file:///c:/Users/shrav/OneDrive/Desktop/MarketingOS2.0/nexus.py))
- **1,447 lines** — the brain of the entire system
- **Smart routing**: analyzes the user's query and picks the best agent(s)
- **Pipeline execution**: chains agents together (e.g., SEO → Content → PPC) in serial or parallel
- **Agent Debate**: when agents disagree, Nexus facilitates structured debate and picks a winner using real GA4 data
- **Budget Manager**: tracks spending across campaigns, approves/denies allocation requests
- **Onboarding**: detects first-time users and collects business profile progressively
- **Performance tracking**: logs which agents are used, latency, and model info

### 2. Model Router ([model_router.py](file:///c:/Users/shrav/OneDrive/Desktop/MarketingOS2.0/model_router.py))
- **846 lines** — unified multi-provider AI routing
- **5 providers** with tiered fallback: Groq → Gemini → OpenRouter → NVIDIA → DeepSeek
- **4 tiers**: Tier 1 (fast/routing), Tier 2 (standard), Tier 3 (advanced + search), Tier 4 (deep reasoning)
- **Failure cache**: automatically skips dead/rate-limited providers for 5 minutes
- **Web search integration**: Brave + Serper dual-engine search with deduplication

### 3. FastAPI Backend ([main.py](file:///c:/Users/shrav/OneDrive/Desktop/MarketingOS2.0/backend/main.py))
- **1,101 lines**, 87+ endpoint handlers
- Full REST API for all agents and integrations
- Key endpoint categories:
  - Health/status checks and provider diagnostics
  - Nexus smart routing (`/api/execute`)
  - Direct agent endpoints (SEO, Content, PPC, Analytics, etc.)
  - Real integration endpoints (Google Ads campaigns, GA4 data, WordPress publishing, HubSpot contacts)
  - Memory/profile management
  - Agent debate and feedback loops

